Feature addition: dynamic enemy cap scales with difficulty on small maps.

This commit modifies 4 files (+104/-2 lines), spanning 1 core game loop, 1 TypeScript source, 1 tests.
This feature extends the Geometry Wars 3D codebase with new functionality. The implementation follows the project's established patterns and maintains compatibility with both single-player and multiplayer code paths where applicable.

Additional context from the commit body:
- Added getDynamicMaxEnemies(size, difficultyLevel) to MapSize.ts
  - Below diff 6: returns static base cap (unchanged)
  - Diff 6+: adds floor((level-6)*5) per level, capped per map size
  - Caps: SMALL=80, MEDIUM=150, LARGE=200, EPIC=250
- main.ts: calls setMaxActiveEnemies() every frame with dynamic cap
  (was called once at startup; now tracks waveScheduler.currentDifficultyLevel)
- 12 unit tests added to difficulty-rebalance.test.ts covering all criteria

